  "scope": "This ledger reports the 2025 Massachusetts Health Insurance Survey for residents and their families: the CHIA high out-of-pocket-to-income ratio, the published share-of-income distribution, any family affordability issue, problems paying medical bills, family medical debt, unmet need due to cost, insurance coverage at the time of the survey, and the high-deductible share among the privately insured. Cuts are the published family-income and race or ethnicity tables. The survey was fielded January through April 2025 and published in December 2025.",
  "exclusions": "Does not publish an average dollar out-of-pocket cost; MHIS does not print that cell. Does not cover hospital relative prices, 340B, Medicaid program expenditures, MEPS Insurance Component family premiums, CMS National Health Expenditure per-capita out-of-pocket spending, other states, or advice about a plan or provider.",
  "heritage": "New. The Tableau suite did not publish the Massachusetts Health Insurance Survey as a namesake.",
  "replaces": [],
  "vintage_note": "Compiled Aug 17, 2026 from the CHIA 2025 MHIS detailed data tables (December 2025). Percents are the published Total and group columns. The high out-of-pocket ratio uses CHIA's threshold: above 5 percent of income below 200 percent FPL, or above 10 percent at or above 200 percent FPL. Two-path check: Excel Total cells match the printed 2025 report shares for coverage, affordability, bills, debt, and unmet need. Ranks among income or race groups are Pioneer calculations (derived).",
