  "data_month_label": "2025 MHIS, fielded January to April 2025",
  "lead": "<b>8.6 percent</b> of Massachusetts residents were in families with a high out-of-pocket healthcare burden in 2025 (SRC-633-02). CHIA counts out-of-pocket costs above 5 percent of income for families below 200 percent of the federal poverty level, or above 10 percent at or above 200 percent. The share was <b>19.2 percent</b> below 139 percent of poverty and <b>2.9 percent</b> at 500 percent or more (SRC-633-02). The survey does not publish an average dollar out-of-pocket cost.",
